1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.393
An algorithm was beating the traders.

2
00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:07.070
And the traders played their hunches anyway.

3
00:00:07.071 --> 00:00:19.116
Talon Outdoor — the UK's largest out-of-home agency — about to become the market's aggregator: a DSP with its own demand side, audience intelligence included.

4
00:00:19.117 --> 00:00:23.161
Five years, six systems, one platform.

5
00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:27.405
The model was right, and ignored.

6
00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:31.143
That wasn't stubbornness — it was rational.

7
00:00:31.144 --> 00:00:36.433
A bare ranked list gives an expert nothing to do with their doubt.

8
00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:42.115
So I stopped sharpening the model, and changed what it handed over.

9
00:00:42.116 --> 00:00:50.221
A ranked list of billboards became a full campaign plan — KP Is attached, customisable in one click.

10
00:00:50.222 --> 00:00:53.087
This is the live reconstruction.

11
00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:57.102
Watch the plan reshape when the priority switches.

12
00:00:57.103 --> 00:00:59.211
ROI first.

13
00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:02.923
Same engine output — a different argument.

14
00:01:02.924 --> 00:01:06.698
One a trader can stake their name on.

15
00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:10.714
Users don't adopt the most accurate system.

16
00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:14.692
They adopt the one that lets them argue back.

17
00:01:15.814 --> 00:01:23.651
Traders could redistribute the media, remove placements, or rewrite the brief and fetch a fresh plan.

18
00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:27.504
No notification told them they'd been heard.

19
00:01:27.505 --> 00:01:33.432
The next plan's numbers did — impressions, reach, cover, frequency.

20
00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:37.014
Campaign planning: two weeks to three hours.

21
00:01:37.015 --> 00:01:43.792
Sixty-nine thousand pounds more media value per client, against trader baselines.

22
00:01:43.793 --> 00:01:55.017
And on the public record, from the client's own leadership: under five percent, to one hundred percent of UK bookings through the platform, in about a year.

23
00:01:55.018 --> 00:02:01.215
The bidding model, and the fifty-million-bids-an-hour infrastructure — engineering's win.

24
00:02:01.216 --> 00:02:03.677
The adoption was mine.

25
00:02:04.798 --> 00:02:11.482
Where this breaks: argue-back needs an accountable expert on the other side.

26
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:14.971
And it can't rescue a weak model.

27
00:02:14.972 --> 00:02:19.422
If either fails in your product, don't copy this.

28
00:02:19.423 --> 00:02:24.958
The principle, and every claim beside its evidence, is below.
